# Call-site ledger of pubchempy at 9935a14e7fdb4a88d27a99fedce69ca99f004698 (v1.0.5).
# Decide every `undecided` line; see macro-benchmark/README.md.
#
# pubchempy has no trace: every edge comes from reading (pubchempy.md).
# Analysed source: pubchempy.py (root "."), one module. Python >= 3.10,
# CPython only (no other implementation is declared), every platform
# ("Operating System :: OS Independent"; CI on Linux, macOS and Windows).
# Optional imports (certifi, pandas) run on both sides. A response of urlopen
# is an http.client.HTTPResponse, or the urllib.response.addinfourl of a
# redirect to an ftp URL (judgement J3).
default reject pubchempy.Atom.__getitem__, pubchempy.Bond.__getitem__: no value subscripted at this site is an Atom or a Bond: the package subscripts the dicts and lists of the parsed JSON records, its own dicts (_atoms, _bonds, ELEMENTS, PROPERTY_MAP, error_map, kwargs), strs and a frozenset key lookup; dict-style access to Atom and Bond is deprecated client API that no package code uses
default reject pubchempy.Atom.__eq__, pubchempy.Bond.__eq__, pubchempy.Compound.__eq__, pubchempy.Substance.__eq__, pubchempy.Assay.__eq__: no operand of this comparison or `in` test, and no key of this dict or set operation, is an Atom, Bond, Compound, Substance or Assay: the operands are str, int, float, None, IntEnum members, dicts and lists of JSON records, frozensets of ints and client keys
default reject pubchempy.Atom.__contains__, pubchempy.Bond.__contains__: no container of this `in` test is an Atom or a Bond: the containers are dicts and lists of the JSON records, dict_items views, str/list/set displays and package dicts; no package code tests membership in an Atom or Bond

